1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,720
Think about this: A claim was filed
yesterday.

2
00:00:03,380 --> 00:00:04,700
What status is established?

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:06,460
Let’s work through it together.

4
00:00:07,080 --> 00:00:12,360
I'm Doctor Gainz. Lesson 12: Track claims,
distributions, and deadlines.

5
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:17,380
A filed motion or claim is not necessarily
an approved distribution.

6
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:22,380
Similarly, an approved distribution may
have been paid, stayed, corrected,

7
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:27,360
or challenged. Keep an event log that
distinguishes filed, pending, ordered,

8
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:30,180
disbursed, and unresolved statuses.

9
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:33,440
Use the language of the source and
preserve any qualification.

10
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:38,160
For each important date, record the
triggering event, the source, and who

11
00:00:38,160 --> 00:00:41,940
confirmed its significance. Flag a
deadline that requires professional

12
00:00:41,940 --> 00:00:46,360
interpretation. Keep status history
instead of overwriting a former amount

13
00:00:46,360 --> 00:00:51,300
without explanation. Where a source is
old, closed, or access-limited, make

14
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:53,680
that limitation visible at the top of the
file.

15
00:00:54,100 --> 00:00:57,100
No general time promise is appropriate for
every claim.

16
00:00:57,580 --> 00:01:01,500
A useful update states what was checked,
when it was checked, what remains

17
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,840
unknown, and the permitted next action.

18
00:01:04,320 --> 00:01:07,700
Avoid telling a client that money is on
its way because a document was

19
00:01:07,700 --> 00:01:10,080
submitted. Pause and try this.

20
00:01:10,620 --> 00:01:14,720
Write a fictional event log containing a
claim, a competing claim, and an

21
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:18,740
unresolved hearing. Draft an accurate two-
sentence status update.

22
00:01:19,440 --> 00:01:22,340
Quick knowledge check. A claim was filed
yesterday.

23
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:24,240
What status is established?

24
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:28,440
The answer: Filed; outcome remains
unverified.

25
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:33,120
Filing records establish that an event
occurred, not that entitlement or

26
00:01:33,120 --> 00:01:37,600
payment was decided. Keep the source, the
date, and the unknowns visible.

27
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:39,320
I'll see you in the next lesson.
